    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d679">

                <pb facs="1229" n="1189" sameAs="frus:frus1951v05/pg1189"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">782.5 MSA/12–2151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Turkey
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d679-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-26T18:51:00-05:00">December 26,
                            1951—6:51 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>552. Re Embtel 560 Dec 21. Paras four<anchor n="2" xml:id="d679-f2"/> and five
                        MSA<anchor n="3" xml:id="d679-f3"/> notes not absolutely required by Act of
                    Cong but as they are being incorporated in agreements with other countries
                    appears necessary for sake of uniformity of treatment to include in agreement
                    with Turk. Failure to include wld greatly increase difficulties in negots in
                    future years.</p>
                <p>Re Para five concerning emigration wld Turk objection be met by inserting phrase
                    in second sentence “for the resettlement of refugees <pb facs="1230" n="1190"
                        xml:id="pg1190"/> within Turk and for” after “include expenditures”. No
                    objection giving Turks formal statement in supplementary <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> along lines Para 2 Deptel 527 Dec 17.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d679-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>Re Para 4 MSA note, exchange of notes can be accomplished by <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> in which US states: <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Turk lira will not be converted into dollars</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>No conversion without prior consultation Turk Govt and Turk fon
                            exchange position will be taken into account</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Use of counterpart for conversions into other currencies will be
                            carried out in Turk and will be limited in magnitude.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
